      "fullText": "Artificial intelligence Trump awards Musk and other tech titans National Medals of Science President Donald Trump joined Michael Kratsios to award the Medal of Science to Elon Musk, Jensen Huang, Lisa Su and Sergey Brin amid announcements about new science funding. Listen to this article with a free profile 00:00 00:00 Tesla and SpaceX CEO Elon Musk receives the National Medal of Science from President Donald Trump at the Science: A New Golden Age Summit at the U.S. Institute of Peace on Thursday. Win McNamee / Getty Share Add NBC News to Google Oct. 8, 2026, 5:43 PM EDT By Jared Perlo WASHINGTON — President Donald Trump joined some of America’s most powerful tech leaders Thursday at a summit the White House billed as the start of a “golden age” of American science. Elon Musk, Google co-founder Sergey Brin, Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang, AMD CEO Lisa Su, Microsoft CEO Satya Nadella and Dell founder Michael Dell gathered with Trump and a host of administration officials and scientific luminaries for the Science: A New Golden Age Summit at the U.S. Institute of Peace. “We live in an age of American wonders and technological marvels, and with the help of the brilliant men and women here today, we will always be on top,” Trump said. Trump awarded the National Medal of Science to Musk, Brin, Huang and Su. He awarded the National Medal of Technology and Innovation to Nadella and Dell. Michael Kratsios, director of the White House Office of Science and Technology Policy, addresses the audience Thursday afternoon at the U.S. Institute of Peace. Jared Perlo / NBC News Trump presented each of the recipients with medals and certificates of honor, later asking some of their families to join him onstage to take photos. “You’re going to go down in the annals of history as being great,” Trump told the recipients. For Subscribers FOR SUBSCRIBERS Inflation and tariffs push U.S. holiday spending projections to a record $1.7 trillion FOR SUBSCRIBERS What happened inside the room where offic"
